  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a bicycle with a historical photograph of two Black men, using the text 'the first one can't sing when you put chains on it' to imply that Black people are incapable of singing when subjected to chains. This is a harmful and racist stereotype that equates Black people with animals and perpetuates the idea that they are incapable of certain cultural expressions under oppression. The image and text together create a toxic and offensive message rooted in historical racism.",
